# D46 — the PARENLESS variant path, pinned in the fast suite.
#
# `Direction.North` without parentheses constructs the same nullary variant as
# `Direction.North()`, but it leaves `unify` with an inference-poisoned result
# type. A gate that judges only the unified type reads "no opinion" and ACCEPTS,
# so `d == Direction.North` compiled and answered address identity while
# `d == e` on the same enum, one line away, was refused. The equality gate
# therefore falls back to the OPERAND types whenever the unified type carries no
# verdict at all.
#
# ⚠ THE PARENTHESES ARE THE WHOLE VARIABLE. Every other reject fixture here
# stays red with the fallback removed; this one does not. Do not "simplify" it
# by adding the parens, and do not fold it into a sibling.
#
# The cross-lane half is `spectests/run/reject_eq_parenless_variant.gg` (ggdef +
# C + LLVM + self-host, all four MATCH). This copy exists so the shape is also
# caught by `cargo test --test integration d46_`, which is what anyone editing
# `eq_comparable_blame` actually runs.
#
# Asserted by `d46_eq_parenless_variant_rejects` in tests/integration.rs.

enum Direction:
    North
    South

void main():
    Direction d = Direction.North
    bool a = d == Direction.North
    print(f"{a}")
